claim.claim-text:
receiving M configuration information blocks via an air interface prior to transmitting a first radio signal (S202, S502), the M configuration information blocks respectively indicating M reference signals;
receiving the M reference signals (S21, S51);
transmitting the first radio signal (S22, S52), the first radio signal indicating a first reference signal out of the M reference signals; and
monitoring a first signaling in each time-frequency resource block of W time-frequency resource block(s) (S23, S53);
wherein any of the M reference signals is a CSI-RS or an SS/PBCH block; measurements on the M reference signals are used to determine the first reference signal; at least one reference signal of the M reference signals is transmitted by a first serving cell, and the first serving cell is not added by the UE; the UE assumes that a transmission antenna port of the first signaling is Quasi-Co-Located with a transmission antenna port of the first reference signal; W is a positive integer, and M is a positive integer greater than 1; the first signaling comprises DCI, CRC of the first signaling is scrambled by a C-RNTI; the first radio signal is transmitted on a second serving cell, and the second serving cell is added by the UE; the first serving cell is not a PCell of the UE; the meaning of the phrase that the first serving cell is not added by the UE includes that the UE is not assigned an SCellIndex nor a ServCellIndex for the first serving cell; the meaning of the phrase that the second serving cell is added by the UE includes that the UE is assigned an SCellIndex or a ServCellIndex for the second serving cell.

a first transmitter (2001), which transmits a first radio signal, the first radio signal indicating a first reference signal out of M reference signals; and
a first receiver (2002), which receives M configuration information blocks via an air interface prior to transmitting the first radio signal, receives the M reference signals and monitors a first signaling in each time-frequency resource block of W time-frequency resource block(s), the M configuration information blocks respectively indicating the M reference signals;
wherein measurements on the M reference signals are used to determine the first reference signal; at least one reference signal of the M reference signals is transmitted by a first serving cell, and the first serving cell is not added by the UE; the UE assumes that a transmission antenna port of the first signaling is Quasi-Co-Located with a transmission antenna port of the first reference signal; W is a positive integer, and M is a positive integer greater than 1; the first signaling comprises DCI, CRC of the first signaling is scrambled by a C-RNTI; the first radio signal is transmitted on a second serving cell, and the second serving cell is added by the UE; the first serving cell is not a PCell of the UE; the meaning of the phrase that the first serving cell is not added by the UE includes that the UE is not assigned an SCellIndex nor a ServCellIndex for the first serving cell; the meaning of the phrase that the second serving cell is added by the UE includes that the UE is assigned an SCellIndex or a ServCellIndex for the second serving cell.

a second receiver (2101), which receives a first radio signal, the first radio signal indicating a first reference signal out of M reference signals; and
a second transmitter (2102), which transmits a first signaling in at least one time-frequency resource block of W time-frequency resource block(s), wherein the first reference signal is transmitted by a serving cell maintained by the first base station; or, which drops transmitting the first signaling in the W time-frequency resource block(s), wherein the first reference signal is not transmitted by any serving cell maintained by the base station;
the second transmitter (2102), which transmits M configuration information blocks via an air interface prior to receiving the first radio signal, the M configuration information blocks respectively indicating the M reference signals;
wherein any of the M reference signals is a CSI-RS or an SS/PBCH block; at least one reference signal of the M reference signals is transmitted by a first serving cell, the first serving cell not being added by a transmitter of the first radio signal; at least one serving cell maintained by the first base station is added by the transmitter of the first radio signal; the transmitter of the first radio signal assumes that a transmission antenna port of the first signaling is Quasi-Co-Located with a transmission antenna port of the first reference signal; W is a positive integer, and M is a positive integer greater than 1; the first signaling comprises DCI; CRC of the first signaling is scrambled by a C-RNTI; the first radio signal is transmitted on a second serving cell, and the second serving cell is added by the transmitter of the first radio signal; the first serving cell is not a PCell of the transmitter of the first radio signal; the meaning of the phrase that the first serving cell is not added by a transmitter of the first radio signal includes that the transmitter of the first radio signal is not assigned an ScellIndex nor a ServCellIndex for the first serving cell; the meaning of the phrase that the second serving cell is added by the transmitter of the first radio signal includes that the transmitter of the first radio signal is assigned an ScellIndex or a ServCellIndex for the second serving cell; the first base station is a TRP.
